---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Acquired"
  description="A personal museum for accessioning meaningful objects with photographs, provenance, catalog records, and the story of why each thing matters."
  ogType="article"
  image={withBase('/og/works/acquired.png')}
>
  <article class="kh-case kh-acquired-case" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="kh-case-head section kh-acquired-head">
      <div>
        <p class="kh-case-kicker">PROJECT / BUILT 2026</p>
        <p class="kh-acquired-number">KH.2026.0006 / PERMANENT COLLECTION</p>
        <h1 class="kh-case-title kh-acquired-title">ACQUIRED</h1>
        <p class="kh-case-deck kh-acquired-deck">
          A personal museum for the things you keep — and why you kept them.
        </p>
        <div class="kh-case-actions">
          <a
            class="kh-pill kh-acquired-primary"
            href="https://iphiginea.github.io/acquired/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Open app ↗
          </a>
          <a
            class="kh-text-link kh-acquired-link"
            href="https://github.com/iphiginea/acquired"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <dl class="kh-case-meta kh-acquired-meta">
        <div>
          <dt>Role</dt>
          <dd>Concept / Product Design / Development</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Focus</dt>
          <dd>Collection systems / Personal archives / Supabase</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Year</dt>
          <dd>2026</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <section class="kh-acquired-visual section" aria-label="Acquired collection record concept">
      <div class="kh-acquired-plate">
        <div class="kh-acquired-plate-top">
          <span>ACQUIRED.</span>
          <span>OBJECT RECORD</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kh-acquired-record-head">
          <div>
            <span class="kh-acquired-label">ACCESSION NUMBER</span>
            <strong>KH.2026.0001</strong>
          </div>
          <span class="kh-acquired-status">PERMANENT COLLECTION</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kh-acquired-object-grid">
          <div class="kh-acquired-object-image" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="kh-acquired-object-shape"></div>
            <span>OBJECT PHOTOGRAPH</span>
          </div>

          <dl class="kh-acquired-object-fields">
            <div>
              <dt>Object title</dt>
              <dd>The thing worth remembering</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Date / period</dt>
              <dd>Recorded as part of the object, not just the upload</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Maker / materials</dt>
              <dd>Structured details that make the record useful later</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Provenance</dt>
              <dd>Where it came from, how it arrived, who had it before</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="kh-acquired-significance-row">
              <dt>Significance</dt>
              <dd>The personal history that turns an object into part of a collection</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="kh-case-body section">
      <aside>
        <p class="kh-case-section-label">PROJECT NOTES</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="kh-case-prose kh-acquired-prose">
        <h2>Your life, in objects</h2>
        <p>
          Acquired started with a museum idea: objects become more meaningful when the information
          around them survives too. We save photographs by the thousands, but the context around a
          physical thing — where it came from, who owned it, why we kept it — is much easier to lose.
        </p>
        <p>
          I wanted a personal collection system that treated those stories with the same seriousness
          a museum gives an accession record, without making the experience feel academic or heavy.
        </p>

        <h2>Accession first, organize second</h2>
        <p>
          Each object receives a collection-specific accession number and a structured record for
          title, date, maker, classification, materials, place, acquisition history, provenance, and
          significance. That gives the collection a durable internal logic instead of depending on
          filenames, folders, or memory.
        </p>
        <p>
          Photographs can be uploaded, cropped for the collection grid, and processed to remove their
          background. Objects can stay private or be made public individually, so the same collection
          can hold both intimate records and things worth sharing.
        </p>

        <h2>A museum language for personal history</h2>
        <p>
          The visual system deliberately borrows from collection catalogs rather than social feeds:
          cream paper tones, archival red, brass accession numbers, serif display type, fine rules,
          and quiet object cards. The interface is meant to make documenting an object feel like an
          act of preservation, not another post.
        </p>

        <h2>Built to keep growing</h2>
        <p>
          Supabase handles account authentication, structured object records, and image storage. The
          collection view is searchable and designed to scale as more objects are accessioned, while
          individual object pages preserve the complete record behind each thumbnail.
        </p>
        <p>
          The point is not to document everything you own. It is to preserve the things whose stories
          would otherwise disappear.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="kh-case-next section kh-acquired-next">
      <a href={withBase('/works/')}>
        <span class="kh-case-section-label">ALL EXPERIMENTS</span>
        <strong>Back to the collection →</strong>
      </a>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .kh-acquired-case {
    --acq-red: #7b1420;
    --acq-red-deep: #5c0f18;
    --acq-cream: #f4f1e9;
    --acq-ink: #171717;
    --acq-brass: #a8874b;
    color: var(--acq-ink);
  }

  .kh-acquired-head {
    position: relative;
  }

  .kh-acquired-number {
    margin: 1.15rem 0 0;
    color: var(--acq-brass);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-acquired-title {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--acq-red);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-acquired-deck {
    max-width: 22ch;
    color: var(--acq-red-deep);
    font-weight: 520;
  }

  .kh-acquired-meta {
    border: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.35);
    background: var(--acq-cream);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 7px var(--acq-cream),
      inset 0 0 0 8px rgba(123, 20, 32, 0.16);
  }

  .kh-acquired-meta dt {
    color: var(--acq-red);
  }

  .kh-acquired-primary {
    border-color: var(--acq-ink);
    background: var(--acq-ink);
    color: var(--acq-cream) !important;
  }

  .kh-acquired-primary:hover,
  .kh-acquired-primary:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--acq-red);
    background: var(--acq-red);
  }

  .kh-acquired-link {
    color: var(--acq-ink);
  }

  .kh-acquired-visual {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
  }

  .kh-acquired-plate {
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.45);
    background: var(--acq-cream);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 8px var(--acq-cream),
      inset 0 0 0 9px rgba(123, 20, 32, 0.18);
  }

  .kh-acquired-plate-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.4rem clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.18);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-acquired-plate-top span:first-child {
    color: var(--acq-red);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .kh-acquired-record-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: end;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.18);
  }

  .kh-acquired-label,
  .kh-acquired-status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.63rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-acquired-record-head strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--acq-brass);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.6rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .kh-acquired-status {
    color: var(--acq-red);
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(16rem, 0.75fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
    gap: 0;
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-image {
    min-height: clamp(24rem, 46vw, 38rem);
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    align-content: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-right: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.18);
    background: #e7e2d5;
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-shape {
    width: min(55%, 14rem);
    aspect-ratio: 0.72;
    border: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.28);
    border-radius: 48% 52% 35% 42% / 28% 30% 70% 72%;
    background:
      linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.78), rgba(168,135,75,0.18)),
      #d3c8ad;
    box-shadow: 1.1rem 1.4rem 0 rgba(123, 20, 32, 0.08);
    transform: rotate(-4deg);
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-image span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    opacity: 0.5;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-fields {
    margin: 0;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-fields div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, 0.42fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 1.15rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.14);
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-fields dt,
  .kh-acquired-object-fields dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-fields dt {
    color: var(--acq-red);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.63rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-fields dd {
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.2vw, 1.08rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .kh-acquired-object-fields .kh-acquired-significance-row {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--acq-red);
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .kh-acquired-significance-row dd {
    color: var(--acq-red-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.8rem);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .kh-acquired-prose h2 {
    color: var(--acq-red);
  }

  .kh-acquired-next {
    border: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.38);
    background: var(--acq-cream);
  }

  .kh-acquired-next a {
    color: var(--acq-red);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .kh-acquired-object-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .kh-acquired-object-image {
      min-height: 22rem;
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.18);
    }

    .kh-acquired-object-fields div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.45rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .kh-acquired-record-head,
    .kh-acquired-plate-top {
      align-items: start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .kh-acquired-title {
      font-size: clamp(4rem, 20vw, 6rem);
    }
  }
</style>
